2026-05-15 01:26:52,425 - INFO - LLM Output: Here are three possible next steps for feature engineering to improve the downstream model's performance:

### Step 1: Identify Suit Uniformity (Flush Detection)
Reasoning: Poker hands like Flush, Straight Flush, and Royal Flush require all cards to have the same suit. Creating a feature to indicate suit uniformity can make it easier for the model to identify these patterns.

1. <suit_diff_1_2>subtract<V1><V3><difference_between_suit_of_card_1_and_card_2>
2. <suit_diff_3_4>subtract<V5><V7><difference_between_suit_of_card_3_and_card_4>
3. <same_suit_all>equal<V1><V3><checks_if_first_two_cards_have_same_suit>
4. <flush_indicator>groupbythenmax<V1><same_suit_all><checks_if_all_cards_have_the_same_suit>

---

### Step 2: Rank Uniformity and Pair Detection
Reasoning: Features like One Pair, Two Pairs, Three of a Kind, and Four of a Kind rely on rank repetition. Calculating rank uniformity will help the model identify these hands.

1. <rank_diff_1_2>subtract<V2><V4><difference_between_rank_of_card_1_and_card_2>
2. <rank_unique_count>groupbythennunique<V2_to_V10><none><number_of_unique_ranks_in_hand>
3. <pair_indicator>equal<rank_unique_count><4><indicates_presence_of_a_single_pair>
4. <three_of_a_kind_indicator>equal<rank_unique_count><3><indicates_three_identical_ranks>

---

### Step 3: Straight Detection (Consecutive Ranks)
Reasoning: Hands like Straights, Straight Flushes, and Royal Flushes rely on cards having sequential ranks. Computing the maximum and minimum ranks will help in detecting these hands (no gaps in rank).

1. <rank_min>groupbythenmin<V1><V10><minimum_rank_in_hand>
2. <rank_max>groupbythenmax<V1><V10><maximum_rank_in_hand>
3. <rank_range>subtract<rank_max><rank_min><range_of_ranks_in_hand>
4. <straight_indicator>equal<rank_range><4><indicates_consecutive_ranks_for_straight_hands>

These features will help the downstream model better predict key poker hands by focusing on suit uniformity (flush detection), rank repetition (pairs, three-of-a-kind, etc.), and rank continuity (straight detection), which are fundamental to identifying poker hands effectively.
